  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B015",
        "laureates": [
          "Akira Ohtomo",
          "Harold Y. Hwang"
        ],
        "citation": "for the discovery of a two-dimensional electron system at oxide heterointerfaces"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B012",
    "B049"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B015 remains my preferred configuration. The LaAlO3/SrTiO3 experiment made an unforeseen interfacial electronic system directly accessible in a material platform, opening sustained experimental work on emergent oxide-interface phases. It is a discrete original discovery rather than recognition for later refinement, has been examined for more than two decades, and connects a clear materials interface to genuinely new electronic behaviour. Ohtomo and Hwang are the two names supplied for the original experiment, a compact attribution that is preferable to crediting a broad subsequent field.",
    "case_against": "The mechanism behind the conducting interface and the division between the original observation, materials preparation, and subsequent interpretation require archival priority review. This is important because the citation must recognize the original discovery, not the later richness of oxide-interface research.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that B012 is a mature, consequential new semiconductor-laser architecture, with Cho, Capasso, and Faist spanning heterostructure technology, the quantum-engineering concept, and realization.",
        "response": "I agree that B012 is an exceptionally strong alternative and have retained it. Its invention and practical impact are unusually clear. My qualification is that the proposed three-person chain mixes an enabling materials platform with the specific cascade invention; the historical boundary must be settled before treating all three contributions as one equally direct original achievement."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson emphasizes that B025 established the physical logic of protecting quantum information and now has meaningful logical-qubit demonstrations.",
        "response": "The foundational importance is unquestionable, but the decisive practical threshold remains unfinished, as Johansson also notes. The ballot also joins codes, fault tolerance, and topological protection into a broad intellectual programme. I would presently prefer an experimentally established, narrowly delimited discovery such as B015."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson identifies B011 as a mature topological-matter achievement combining Kane and Mele's framework with Molenkamp's landmark experiment.",
        "response": "That theory-experiment combination is compelling and mature. However, the supplied assessment itself indicates wider essential contributors, whereas B015 presently offers a more bounded original interface experiment and a two-person attribution that can be tested directly against the historical record."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the original LaAlO3/SrTiO3 observation can be separated cleanly from later explanations of its carrier source and emergent phases.",
      "Whether the supplied credited pair exhausts the original experimental attribution."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
